A good structure is to put fetching behind one client/service layer and cache successful responses so repeated requests can reuse them. For I/O-bound calls, use async requests or a thread pool to overlap network waits; use a concurrency limit so you don’t overwhelm the API. If the cache must be shared across app processes or survive restarts, use Redis or a database rather than an in-memory dictionary.

